-- title:
--   Order zero of the Hecke multiplier away from j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $N,\ell$ be nonzero naturals with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $q\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq q$. Inside $k((t))$ write $F_N$ for `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the $k$-subfield generated by the Laurent series $j$ and its $N$-fold substitution, and $R$ for `charLDegeneracyRoof k N ℓ`, the $k$-subfield generated by $j$ and its $N$-, $\ell$- and $N\ell$-fold substitutions; let $\bar\jmath =$ `jGeomGen k N` $\in F_N$ be the first of these. Two $k$-algebra maps $F_N\to R$ are in play: $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC k N ℓ`, the inclusion, and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC k N ℓ`, induced by the substitution $t\mapsto t^{\ell}$. Assume both are integral on underlying ring homomorphisms, that $F_N$ is algebraic over $k(\bar\jmath)$ and that $R$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield generated by $\alpha(\bar\jmath)$. Let $h\in R$ satisfy $D(\beta(\bar\jmath)) = h\cdot \alpha_{*}\,D(\bar\jmath)$ in $\Omega_{R/k}$, where $\alpha_{*}$ is the map `pullbackDiff` on Kähler differentials induced by $\alpha$, and assume $D(\alpha(\bar\jmath))\neq 0$ and $D(\beta(\bar\jmath))\neq 0$. Let $y$ be a place of $R$ over $k$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $R$ containing $k$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring, and suppose $\alpha(\bar\jmath)$ and $\beta(\bar\jmath)$ both lie in that valuation subring and that each of their residues in $k$, via `Place.evalAt`, is different from $0$ and from $1728$. Then $y.\mathrm{ord}\,h = 0$, the order being minus the logarithm of the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation attached to $y$.
--
--   This is the generic case of the order formula for the multiplier $h$ relating the two degeneracy maps from the $\ell$-degeneracy roof to the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $q$: when the two $j$-values at $y$, the $j$-invariants of an $\ell$-isogenous pair, avoid $0$ and $1728$, all the relevant covers are unramified at $y$ and $h$ is a unit there. It refines [`ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq) and feeds [`ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq_of_ord_neg_of_eq_smul_map`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_heckeMultiplier_eq_of_ord_neg_of_eq_smul_map), used in the description of the Hecke action on the special fibre at level $N$.
